{"issue": true, "summary": "In the `getParser` method, when a parser is found via regex matching, it retrieves the parser using `parserRegExp.toString()` as the key instead of the actual RegExp object, which can cause cache misses and incorrect parser selection.", "edits": [{"path": "lib/content-type-parser.js", "old": "    if (parserRegExp.test(ct)) {
      parser = this.customParsers.get(parserRegExp.toString())
      this.cache.set(ct, parser)
      return parser
    }", "new": "    if (parserRegExp.test(ct)) {
      parser = this.customParsers.get(parserRegExp)
      this.cache.set(ct, parser)
      return parser
    }"}]}
